2026-10-28T17:16:35.3008902Z {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BgKapQCcus6wqr9DDbQRt5","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"issue\": {\n    \"number\": 6,\n    \"title\": \"aws_servicecatalog_portfolio search by name, return id\",\n    \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n    \"labels_at_open\": [\n      \"enhancement\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"as_of\": \"2026-08-03T12:26:08+00:00\",\n  \"form\": {\n    \"template\": \"Request an Enhancement\",\n    \"missing_required\": [],\n    \"empty_optional\": [],\n    \"used_form\": true\n  },\n  \"services\": {\n    \"resources_mentioned\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"aws_servicecatalog_portfolio\",\n        \"resource_exists\": true,\n        \"data_source_exists\": true,\n        \"service_label\": \"service/servicecatalog\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"aws_servicecatalog_product_portfolio_association\",\n        \"resource_exists\": true,\n        \"data_source_exists\": false,\n        \"service_label\": \"service/servicecatalog\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"regex_labeler_would_apply\": [\n      \"service/servicecatalog\"\n    ],\n    \"primary_service_label\": \"service/servicecatalog\"\n  },\n  \"versions\": {\n    \"terraform\": null,\n    \"provider\": null,\n    \"latest_release\": \"6.57.1\",\n    \"latest_release_date\": \"2026-07-29\",\n    \"provider_status\": \"not_reported\",\n    \"newer_release_notes\": [],\n    \"newer_fixes\": []\n  },\n  \"similar_issues\": [\n    {\n      \"number\": 36001,\n      \"ref\": \"hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws#36001\",\n      \"title\": \"[Enhancement]: Provide a way to retrieve the id of the default Sagemaker Service Catalog portfolio \",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"As a user of Sagemaker, I would like to be able to provision new Sagemaker Domains via Terraform which use a custom default execution role that has access to the default service catalog portfolio which AWS provides. While I can enable this portfolio with the aws_sagemaker_servicecatalog_portfolio_status resource, it does not return the portfolio ID required to grant my custom IAM role access to th\",\n      \"state\": \"closed\",\n      \"state_reason\": \"not_planned\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2024-02-28T10:16:50Z\",\n      \"score\": 0.338,\n      \"band\": \"possible\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 37956,\n      \"ref\": \"hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws#37956\",\n      \"title\": \"[Bug]: multiple aws_servicecatalog_provisioning_artifacts can't be created in parallel\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"1.8.3 5.53.0 * aws_servicecatalog_provisioning_artifact All provisioning artifacts get created. Terraform performs CreateProvisioningArtifacts and receives an artifact id and info that it's status is still CREATING, but trying to lookup the status of all but the first artifact later results in ResourceNotFoundException. Only the first artifact gets created. shell ~/tftest$ terraform apply Terrafor\",\n      \"state\": \"closed\",\n      \"state_reason\": \"not_planned\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2024-06-13T14:41:42Z\",\n      \"score\": 0.278,\n      \"band\": \"weak\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 39861,\n      \"ref\": \"hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws#39861\",\n      \"title\": \"[Bug]: aws_servicecatalog_portfolio_share does not support sharing to GovCloud organization\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"latest v5.72.1 aws_servicecatalog_portfolio_share Use aws_servicecatalog_portfolio_share to share a servicecatalog portfolio to a GovCloud organization **(partition is aws-us-gov rather than aws)** using either the organization arn or organization id. hcl # MUST BE RUN FROM A GOVCLOUD ORGANIZATION MANAGEMENT ACCOUNT TO REPRODUCE resource \\\"aws_servicecatalog_organizations_access\\\" \\\"svc_ctlg_orgs_acc\",\n      \"state\": \"closed\",\n      \"state_reason\": \"completed\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2024-10-23T18:07:32Z\",\n      \"score\": 0.236,\n      \"band\": \"weak\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 28348,\n      \"ref\": \"hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws#28348\",\n      \"title\": \"[Bug]: aws_sagemaker_servicecatalog_portfolio_status id attribute returns a region name instead of a portfolio id\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"1.3.5 4.46.0 * aws_sagemaker_servicecatalog_portfolio_status This issue is a follow-up to the recent addition of the aws_sagemaker_servicecatalog_portfolio_status resource. As pointed out in [this comment]( the portfolio share created by the enable sagemaker service catalog portfolio API call may need to be associated with a principal. This is needed to access the resources defined inside the shar\",\n      \"state\": \"open\",\n      \"state_reason\": null,\n      \"created_at\": \"2022-12-14T10:26:25Z\",\n      \"score\": 0.232,\n      \"band\": \"weak\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"number\": 33063,\n      \"ref\": \"hashicorp/terraform-provider-aws#33063\",\n      \"title\": \"[Enhancement]: aws_servicecatalog_tag_option data source\",\n      \"body_excerpt\": \"AWS service catalog tag options are unique key, value pairs. In order to be able to effectively use these across multiple workspaces it is necessary to be able to lookup the associated id of the tag option to assign it to a product or portfolio. This is not possible at present as there is no data source associated with the service catalog tag options. The enhancement is to implement this. The data\",\n      \"state\": \"closed\",\n      \"state_reason\": \"not_planned\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2023-08-17T08:46:54Z\",\n      \"score\": 0.163,\n      \"band\": \"weak\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"corpus_size\": 11477,\n  \"thresholds\": {\n    \"likely\": 0.4,\n    \"possible\": 0.28\n  }\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"93d8758e-1e70-4cef-916c-a61bab462e29","uuid":"5e05997a-166c-42df-83c7-3e6b5c05dd96","timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:16:35.292Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\n  \"issue\": {\n    \"number\": 6,\n    \"title\": \"aws_servicecatalog_portfolio search by name, return 